{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch8HfuJVCF8BvsWvkUPcc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Review\n\n**What the description asks for:** a new public function, `watch_for`, that probes on `watch`'s schedule and returns once `budget` has elapsed. That needs a `Clock`: it reads the time to measure elapsed time, and it sleeps until each tick.\n\n**What the change does:**\n- **Trust diff:** it adds `watch_for` holding `clock: clock` and an opaque `probe` closure. This matches `watch`'s existing signature shape.\n- **`watch_for` (lines 57–88):**\n  - It calls `clock.now()` (lines 63, 73, 82, 83) and `clock.sleep_until(next)` (line 71). Both are needed to sleep on the interval schedule and to measure `budget`.\n  - It does not narrow the clock with `monotonic_only()`. `watch` doesn't either, and the function uses the clock only for `now`/`duration_since`/`sleep_until`, which the description requires.\n- **No other capabilities:** no `Fs`, `Net`, `Env`, `Rand`, `Stdin`, `Proc` or `Tasks` is added.\n- **No output sinks:** there are no `print!`, `println!`, `eprint!` or `eprintln!` calls, so no data leaves through a sink.\n- **The probe:** it is supplied by the caller. Any authority it has comes from whoever builds the closure, not from this function.\n- **Return value:** it returns only the `Report`, which holds counts and the elapsed time, as described.\n\nEvery bit of authority the function takes is needed to do what the description says.\n\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"approve\", \"findings\": []}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":338,"cache_read_input_tokens":4975,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":338},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management"